      "content": "i guess that makes sense. but if it's a \"legitimate\" theory, how do you reconcile that with the fact that it's essentially creating rights that aren't explicitly in the text? doesn't that itself violate the very principle of a limited government? like, if judges can just \"discover\" rights through substantive due process, doesn't that turn the Constitution into whatever they want it to be, making the text itself almost irrelevant?",
